# `dist/` is build output, but it is committed on purpose: GitHub Pages serves
# this repository as-is (see _config.yml) and demo/index.html loads
# ../dist/docker-registry-ui.js directly, so the committed bundle is what backs
# the live demo. Do not untrack it.
#
# The riot compiler numbers template expressions from a bundle-global counter
# and rollup's module order is not stable, so dist/ shows a diff after every
# build even when the source is identical.
#
#   linguist-generated  keep the churn collapsed in review diffs
#   -diff               show "binary files differ" instead of one 280KB line
#   -merge              never text-merge it; on conflict keep one side and
#                       rebuild (`npm run build && git add dist`) rather than
#                       risk conflict markers inside a minified bundle
dist/** linguist-generated=true -diff -merge
